        {
          "file": "proj/src/kbd.c",
          "originalSha256": "0631486b512c5abcd0e3d50d202875900f9063f3fee43a26a53873daa9a44271",
          "patchedSha256": "0c685d3159cce97b6a152efddead7c5be5cc86715049f8d2bf3f2d10224b599c",
          "reason": "Each IRQ device must retain its own handle; shared/shadowed hook_id caused incorrect masks and leaked subscriptions.",
          "verification": "Actual timer, keyboard and mouse driver objects exercised for two subscription/removal rounds; masks identify their independent device handles and all subscriptions are released. Evidence c/bow-hooks-red.log and corresponding green log."
        },
        {
          "file": "proj/src/main.c",
          "originalSha256": "2f1a31e7a0cda8103ac96b5bb68be90504afe85baf7d29d7b12359a83b5e1881",
          "patchedSha256": "5a241291f3e888f0eb96d0ea481688e93ecaee47240ab87dd6141a72f5f507c6",
          "reason": "Include the owning graphics and Minix SEF headers so pointer and startup calls use their real declarations. An undeclared sef_startup call assumed int while the Minix API returns void, producing an immediate WASM signature trap.",
          "verification": "Actual current final browser export trapped in $main before graphics with wasm-ld sef_startup ()->i32 versus ()->void. Actual entry strict compilation fails on the missing declaration; corrected entry executes ordered SEF startup, mode0x117, menu selection and graphics exit. Canonical browser tile/menu/play/Home is rechecked after rebuilding only this game. Evidence build/arcade-100/a/bow-final-diagnosis."
        },
        {
          "file": "proj/src/mouse.c",
          "originalSha256": "58acded3bb14bc73964f041ea79eefdce2a7c322920deebd1eb0b0cc54176a41",
